bank   Maze chase
clock  1512000
tick   220

category Movement

sound Waka, low
audf  90 1 +14 6
audc  202 1 0 6
amp   0.32
note  The eating loop is two alternating blips, played over and over while the stick is
note  held. Distortion 6 is the 4-bit poly -- short enough to repeat inside one blip, which
note  gives it a buzz rather than a tone.

sound Waka, high
audf  60 1 -10 6
audc  202 1 0 6
amp   0.32
note  The other half. Low then high, back and forth, and the pair is the whole sound.

category Pickups

sound Power pellet
audf  120 2 -4 24
audc  202 2 0 24
amp   0.38
note  The rising sibling of the waka, four times as long. Same distortion so it belongs to
note  the same family, which is most of why the original's set sounds coherent.

sound Fruit
audf  100 1 -3 12
audc  170 1 0 12
amp   0.35
note  Pure tone this time, and the only sweet sound in the bank.

sound Eat ghost
audf  200 1 -8 22
audc  170 1 0 22
amp   0.42
note  A long climb from very low. The original slides up nearly two octaves while the
note  ghost's eyes retreat, and the length is doing the work rather than the pitch.

category States

sound Siren
audf  150 3 -6 16
audc  40 3 0 16
amp   0.28
note  The pursuit loop. Distortion 1 is the 5-bit poly -- coarse, but it repeats every 31
note  steps, so it stays pitched instead of turning into hiss.

sound Death
audf  30 2 +9 26
audc  41 2 0 26
amp   0.5
note  Down and coarse, which is what every arcade death is. The 5-bit poly keeps it
note  musical at the bottom of the fall where noise would just be a thud.

sound Extra life
audf  70 1 -6 10
audc  170 1 0 10
amp   0.4
note  Short, high, rising. A reward is always up.

category Interface

sound Credit
audf  80 1 0 3
audc  169 1 0 4
amp   0.35
note  The coin. Two hundredths of a second and the most important sound in the cabinet.
